From: QEMU Anti-Detection Patches
Date: 2025
Subject: [PATCH] target/i386: Hide KVM hypervisor presence when expose_kvm is disabled

When the user sets "-cpu host,-kvm" (expose_kvm=false), also clear the
CPUID[1].ECX[31] hypervisor bit and suppress all Hyper-V CPUID leaves
at 0x40000000.

The original code only cleared FEAT_KVM; the hypervisor bit in FEAT_1_ECX
was left set from the unconditional set in x86_cpu_load_model() or from
the host passthrough feature expansion.  Additionally, if hv-* flags were
enabled, hyperv_fill_cpuids() would still populate the 0x40000000 Hyper-V
CPUID leaves with the configured hv-vendor-id.

Without this patch, even with "-cpu host,-kvm,-hypervisor" and hv-* flags,
the 0x40000000 leaf range can still be discovered by the guest.

---
 target/i386/cpu.c    | 1 +
 target/i386/kvm/kvm.c | 8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/target/i386/cpu.c b/target/i386/cpu.c
index abcdef1..1234567 100644
--- a/target/i386/cpu.c
+++ b/target/i386/cpu.c
@@ -9762,6 +9762,7 @@
 
     if (!kvm_enabled() || !cpu->expose_kvm) {
         env->features[FEAT_KVM] = 0;
+        env->features[FEAT_1_ECX] &= ~CPUID_EXT_HYPERVISOR;
     }
 
     /*
diff --git a/target/i386/kvm/kvm.c b/target/i386/kvm/kvm.c
index abcdef2..2345678 100644
--- a/target/i386/kvm/kvm.c
+++ b/target/i386/kvm/kvm.c
@@ -2290,7 +2290,15 @@ int kvm_arch_init_vcpu(CPUState *cs)
         return -ENOSYS;
     }

-    if (hyperv_enabled(cpu)) {
+    /*
+     * When expose_kvm is disabled, suppress all Hyper-V CPUID leaves
+     * (0x40000000 range) to fully hide the hypervisor presence.  Even
+     * if hv-* flags are set, do not populate the 0x40000000 leaves
+     * as they would reveal a hypervisor vendor ID (e.g. "dkvm") to the
+     * guest.
+     */
+    if (hyperv_enabled(cpu) &&
+        kvm_enabled() && cpu->expose_kvm) {
         r = hyperv_init_vcpu(cpu);
         if (r) {
             return r;
-- 
2.43.0
